BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Peeping Tom — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261112T200000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261115T190000
DTSTAMP:20261102T061401Z
UID:e30b533cc864560f42176da9c9dd@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:Five figures are trapped in a temporal maze\, mutating and col
 liding in an attempt to defy immortality. Their existence takes place in a
  vast sulfuric landscape\, unfolding in a series of chronicles. Is this la
 ndscape the ground for new creations\, or made out of remnants of what onc
 e existed? Confronted with different laws and physical phenomena\, their b
 odies reveal other behaviors and possibilities of being\, without knowing 
 if they are at the twilight or dawn of their existence. We are witnessing 
 a bodily metamorphosis in an abyssal and poetic dimension.\nCategory: Mult
 idisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedul
 e/peeping-tom
LOCATION:Centro Danza Matadero\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/peeping-tom
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roundtable on Contemporary Literature: 'Flesh\, Blood\, and Territ
 ory' — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261112T220000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261112T220000
DTSTAMP:20261102T061401Z
UID:bc3068de89e441a6f44e5161484b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:A panel discussion featuring prominent voices in contemporary 
 speculative literature in Spanish: Mariana Enríquez (Argentina)\, a leadi
 ng figure in Latin American horror and Gothic fiction and author of Our Sh
 are of Night \; Mónica Ojeda (Ecuador)\, author of Jawbone and Las Volado
 ras \, key works of Andean Gothic\; María Fernanda Ampuero (Ecuador)\, jo
 urnalist and writer of visceral\, dark fiction\, author of Cockfight \; an
 d Claudia Amador (Colombia)\, a refreshing voice in Tropical Gothic and cl
 assic genre myths\, author of Altasangre . Moderated by Susana Vallejo (Sp
 ain)\, fantasy and science fiction writer\, author of the Porta Coeli saga
 . Organized by: Besarilia Cultural Association ( Asociación Cu\nCategory:
  Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/sc
 hedule/roundtable-contemporary-literature-flesh-blood-and-territory
LOCATION:Casa del Lector\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/roundtable-contemporary-lit
 erature-flesh-blood-and-territory
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
